# 04-Plot_community_abundance.R
#
# Community/species-group abundance relationship plots paralleling
# Management_plus_HumanCov_relations.jpg (all groups x all covariates,
# unfiltered by statistical support), generated by 04-Plot_community_relations.R
# for Hill-Shannon diversity. Produced for Appendix S3, in response to the
# Editor/Reviewer 3 request (EAP25-0577, 2nd review) to report community-level
# abundance alongside diversity.
#
# Group abundance is the geometric mean, across the species in a group, of
# species-level predicted density (N.pred.calc output, birds/km^2, already
# incorporating each species' own cluster size and effective detection area).
# The geometric mean is used rather than the arithmetic mean because it keeps
# the aggregation on a common density scale across species that differ in
# effective detection area (see prototype comparison,
# archive/04-Plot_community_abundance_prototype_20260828.R, for the
# arithmetic-mean alternative and the reasoning). Only total relationships are
# shown (no human-traffic-explained/unexplained decomposition): unlike the
# diversity relationships, the explained-vs-total pattern for abundance did
# not consistently mirror the diversity relationships' pattern, so that
# decomposition is omitted here to avoid an interpretation this manuscript
# does not need.

